{{Quote|Anything from the Mayor's majordomo? Is he cooperating?''"<br />"''Oh, he's singing like a Yuzzum.|[[Boba Fett]] and [[Fennec Shand]]|<ref name="Gathering Storm">{{BOBF|Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm}}</ref>}}
'''Yuzzums''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[Endor|Forest Moon]] of [[Endor (planet)|Endor]]. A Yuzzum named [[Joh Yowza]] occasionally [[Musician|sang]] with the [[Max Rebo Band]], while another known as [[Wam Lufba]] worked as an exterminator.

==Biology and appearance==
A [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]],<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> Yuzzums were shaggy,<ref name="Joh Yowza">{{Databank|joh-yowza|Joh Yowza}}</ref> [[Hair|fur]]-covered bipeds with rotund bodies,<ref name="Return of the Jedi" /> whose long [[Limb|legs]] allowed them to run fast and catch prey on [[Endor]]'s plains.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> They also had a pair of skinny arms ending in four-fingered hands, two forward-facing [[eye]]s located at the top of their skull, and antenna-like [[ear]]s. The [[mouth]] of a Yuzzum was wide and filled with blunted [[Tooth|teeth]].<ref name="Return of the Jedi" /> Thanks to their rangy limbs, they were taller than [[Ewok]]s.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" />

==Society and culture==
[[File:Yowza_Jedi_Rocks.png|thumb|left|225px|Joh Yowza, a Yuzzum singer]]
Described as "dreamy wanderers,"<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> Yuzzums only used the most basic tools, unlike the Ewoks, who had advanced stone-age technology. They tamed and rode [[rakazzak beast]]s to help them hunt "[[rugger]]," rodents that hid in tall [[grass]]es, which they enjoyed roasted.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" /> Yuzzums spoke the [[language]] of the [[Yuzzum (language)|same name]],<ref name="Complete Locations" /> and were impressive [[Musician|singers]].<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" /> They brewed a [[Yuzzum wine|potent]] [[wine]] that non-Yuzzums could only safely consume when mixed with the simpler, sweeter wine of the Ewoks.<ref name="Wine in Dreams">{{StoryCite|story=The Wine in Dreams|book=Canto Bight (novella collection)}}</ref>

==Yuzzums in the galaxy==
Native to the plains of the [[Forest]] [[Moon]] of [[Endor (planet)|Endor]], some Yuzzums left their [[homeworld]] on passing [[starship]]s and founded populations on other worlds.<ref name="Complete Locations" /> Long before the [[Imperial Era]], a Yuzzum was present during the arrest of [[Darth Momin|Momin]].<ref name="DLOTS 22">[[Darth Vader (2017) 22|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 22]]</ref> By the [[Standard year|year]] [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> a Yuzzum singer named [[Joh Yowza]] performed with the [[Max Rebo Band]] at [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's Palace]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]],<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" /> while another known as [[Wam Lufba]] worked there as an exterminator.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Restitdesigning.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Yuzzum concept art.]]
The Yuzzums were created for the [[1983]] movie [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']], the last installment in the [[original trilogy]] of ''[[Star Wars]]''. Originally, they were meant to be featured in the movie as a companion species to the Ewoks on Endor. However, they proved too costly to produce in quantity. As a consequence, only one Yuzzum puppet was built, and it found its way into the background of Jabba the Hutt's palace. When an extended musical number was added in the [[The Star Wars Trilogy Special Edition|Special Edition]] of ''Return of the Jedi'' in [[1997]], the Yuzzum design was revisited through a computer-generated creation.<ref name="Joh Yowza DB">{{DB|character|johyowza|Yowza, Joh}}</ref>

In the [[2018]] replica journal ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Tales from Vandor]]'', written by [[Jason Fry]], the Yuzzum are included in a list of "big bruiser species," along with the [[Wookiee]]s, [[Houk]]s, and [[Gigoran]]s.<ref name="Tales from Vandor">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Tales from Vandor]]''</ref> Fry, however, has admitted that he actually meant [[Yuzzem]],<ref name="JCF">{{JCFCite|url=posts/55392497|board=Literature|thread=Tales from Vandor by Jason Fry|user=[[Jason Fry|jasonfry]]|date=2018-10-22|time=11:48 AM|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200220204930/https://boards.theforce.net/threads/tales-from-vandor-by-jason-fry.50049692/page-2}}</ref> the large furry humanoids that first appeared in the [[1978]] [[Star Wars Legends|Legends]] novel ''[[Splinter of the Mind's Eye]]''.<ref name="SotME">''[[Splinter of the Mind's Eye]]''</ref>

